## Purpose

Continue the maintainer-directed design reassessment after #588 / draft #589. Start with the central requirement: trustworthy query-result shapes over imperfect schemas and other writers, without silently repairing unexpected data.

## Deliverable

A bounded source-and-existing-test assessment of current validated query-result behavior, plus concrete acceptance tasks for evaluating alternatives. Distinguish:

- result-shape guarantees from policies about accepted input representations;
- declared storage decoding/normalization from permissive coercion;
- model, scalar/computed, named, raw, streaming and RETURNING paths;
- absent rows, stored NULL, query-induced NULL and unchecked reads;
- source observations, existing test assertions and newly executed evidence.

Identify strengths as well as gaps, prioritize the next design decision, and record evidence/limits. Do not present static checks as runtime proof or assume that all Pydantic validation is lax/strict uniformly.

Related but separate: #579 explores boolean/integer semantics; #556 explores additional development/staging verification. Do not implement or independently select their policies here.

## Scope

Assessment and task design only. No production/dependency changes, new public syntax, checker changes, migration work, model/template execution, backend suites or benchmark implementation. Leave draft #589 unmerged unless the maintainer explicitly requests a merge. Any later behavioral prototype requires separately scoped TDD and appropriate native validation.
